---
// Women's Trauma IOP, "What is trauma?". White card, sage border: a ripple from one event (or many) out to the four
// areas of well-being trauma can affect.
// Simplified 2026-11-18 (user: graphics too busy): few big elements, large icon circles, little text, in the style
// of conditions/OcdGraphic.astro and the DBT wheel. Facts are in the bullets beside it. Styles: programs.css (.gx-*).
---
<figure class="gx t-paper a-sage" aria-label="Trauma, from a single event or many, can have lasting effects on physical, social, emotional and spiritual well-being">
  <svg class="gx-svg" viewBox="0 0 320 250" aria-hidden="true">
    <circle cx="160" cy="125" r="108" class="rp r0" /><circle cx="160" cy="125" r="80" class="rp r1" /><circle cx="160" cy="125" r="52" class="rp r2" />
    <circle cx="160" cy="125" r="38" class="core" /><text x="160" y="130" class="cw">Trauma</text>
    {[["Physical", 160, 18], ["Social", 270, 125], ["Emotional", 160, 232], ["Spiritual", 50, 125]].map(([t, x, y]) => (
      <g><rect x={Number(x) - 48} y={Number(y) - 15} width="96" height="30" rx="15" class="lb" /><text x={x} y={Number(y) + 5}>{t}</text></g>
    ))}
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="gx-cap">One event or many, with effects that can last</figcaption>
</figure>
